    "explanation": "To both parties: this is a metered RYDE_X trip (TRP-09111, 18 Sep 2026). The same trip identifier appears on the trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown, and the trace opens at the recorded start time, so the artifacts describe this trip.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED, BUT NOT MATERIAL. The governing figure is the trace length, not the trip record's rounded copy: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 16.2 km (EV-GPS-09111) against the booking-time optimal of 12.0 km (EV-TRIP-09111), an excess of 4.2 km = 35% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (over 0.8 km and over 20%) pass. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 205 fixes at a 10-second interval, coverage 100%, no gaps, no jump over 500 m and no sampling interval over 30 s, so POL-RD-07 does not bite and the finding may rest on the trace alone. Materiality, however, requires an excess over 50% of optimal or over 8.0 km; at 35% and 4.2 km neither is met, so POL-RD-06 is NOT engaged and no driver_profile check, FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral attaches (I record that the profile shows deviation_flags_90d 0 against 610 completed trips, and that the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used).\n\nTHE REFUND IS ARITHMETIC (POL-RD-02; the fare is METERED with a null quoted fare, so POL-RD-11 does not apply). charged_total = SGD 33.36. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 12.0 km + 0.28 x 24.0 min) x 1.2 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 for the on-optimal-route Pioneer Road inbound gantry - 1.00 promo = SGD 24.2240. Refund = 33.36 - 24.2240 = SGD 9.1360, rounded UP to SGD 9.15. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, and it is 27.4% of the charge, far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a partial refund and not a full one. The figure equals the amount you contested, rider.\n\nTHE 'EXTRA ERP' IS ANSWERED INSIDE THAT FIGURE, NOT ON TOP OF IT. The fare's SGD 3.00 of ERP is the SGD 1.00 Pioneer Road inbound gantry (on the optimal route and properly chargeable) plus the SGD 2.00 Tuas South Avenue 8 loop gantry (off the optimal route). The recomputed fare already rebuilds the trip without the off-route gantry, so that SGD 2.00 is comprehended in the SGD 9.15 and must never be added again (POL-RD-09(1)); the on-route gantry correctly stays in.\n\nNOTHING REDUCES OR EXCUSES THE EXCESS. There is no rider-requested detour: the chat log contains only the rider asking the driver to return to the booked route and the driver naming no actable road, and no message carries a waypoint_hint, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable. No endpoint was amended (the amended fields are null), so POL-RD-05 excuses nothing. The only traffic advisory in the bundle (EV-ADVIS-09111-01) carries no payload, so POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing. The driver's statement that he 'followed the road available to me' is a general assertion citing no artifact and no clause, and carries no weight under POL-RD-08; on the record the excess stands unexplained.\n\nNo referral is made. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (so POL-RD-06(c) does not fire), and the off-route ERP is a pass-through item comprehended in the distance refund rather than a billing-integrity defect requiring a POL-RD-09(4) reference. The disputed amount is settled as a partial refund; no escalation is triggered."
