    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this is trip TRP-09111, a metered fare, and the outcome is fixed by the policy arithmetic rather than by discretion.\n\nROUTE. The governing distance is the GPS trace: it runs 16.2 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a platform optimal of 12.0 km. POL-RD-01 provides that where gps_trace.trace_distance_km and trip_record.actual_distance_km disagree the trace governs; the trip record's 16.2 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement and cannot be used for the threshold test. The excess is 4.2 km, or 35.0% of optimal. That passes both establishment gates (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%), so a deviation is established. It passes neither materiality gate (more than 50% or more than 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile review is not triggered; in any event the only fields POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 permit for that test show no pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 610), and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only.\n\nEXONERATION. None applies. The only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09111-01) carries no payload, so POL-RD-03 has no named road, validity window or alternative route to work on and exonerates nothing. The chat log (EV-CHAT-09111) shows the rider asking the driver to return to the booked route at 08:12, with no waypoint and no rider instruction to detour, so POL-RD-04 does not reduce the excess (and your counterparty statement that no stop was requested is consistent with that). No pickup or dropoff was amended and no amended optimal exists, so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11's bar on distance refunds does not apply and POL-RD-02 runs.\n\nREFUND. Charged total is 33.36. The recomputed fare is ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 12.0 optimal km + 0.28 x 24.0 optimal min) x the 1.2 surge read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 for the on-optimal-route Pioneer Road inbound gantry - 1.00 promo = 24.2240. The refund is 33.36 - 24.2240 = 9.1360, rounded up to SGD 9.15. That is 27.4% of the charge, below the 90% full-refund share, and above the SGD 0.50 de minimis: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 9.15, which is the whole of the amount contested.\n\nTHE EXTRA ERP. The fare carries 3.00 of ERP. The 1.00 Pioneer Road inbound gantry lies on the optimal route (the trip record carries it as optimal_route_erp_sgd) and is properly chargeable, so it stays inside the recomputed fare. The 2.00 Tuas South Avenue 8 loop line is off the optimal route and, on the trace, no fix comes within the 250 m match radius of that gantry (nearest fix 1,645.7 m), so the vehicle never passed it; that is a billing-integrity defect recorded for review. The money is not doubled: POL-RD-09(1) provides that off-route ERP is already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 figure and must never be added on top, so the 2.00 is returned inside the 9.15 and is not paid a second time.\n\nEVIDENCE WEIGHT. The facts that decide the case - the excess and the refund - are carried by the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown, none of which is impaired. The trace is clean for policy purposes (205 fixes at a 10 s interval, no gap, full coverage), so POL-RD-07 corroboration is not required and the rider's extra corroboration point is moot. The ruling is therefore not capped below the platform floor."
